---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — keysprint';
const description =
	'The keysprint privacy policy: your typing results stay in your browser, while Google Analytics measures page traffic. Here is what is stored and what is not.';

const updated = '23 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title={title}
	description={description}
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]}
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-6 pt-6 sm:px-6">
		<Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]} />
	</div>

	<PageHero
		eyebrow="Privacy"
		title="Privacy policy"
		lead="keysprint has no accounts and no advertising. Your typing results stay in your browser. Google Analytics measures page traffic, and this page explains exactly what that means."
	/>

	<ContentSection title="The short version">
		<p>
			keysprint does not ask for your name, email address or any other contact details. Your best typing
			score for each test length and your light or dark theme choice are written to your own browser's local
			storage. We also use Google Analytics 4 to count page views and understand which pages are useful.
			Google may set cookies and process technical information about your visit, as described below. Your
			keystrokes and typing results are never sent to Google Analytics.
		</p>
		<Callout title="Your typing results stay on your device" variant="important">
			<p>
				The typing test runs entirely on your machine. The passages are generated locally, your keystrokes
				are measured locally, and your score is calculated locally. The score is not transmitted to a
				server. Google Analytics receives page-level traffic data, not what you type.
			</p>
		</Callout>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="What is stored, and where">
		<p>
			Two pieces of information are kept in your browser's local storage. Local storage stays on your
			device and is not sent to any server, not even by the site that wrote it. Google Analytics also uses
			cookies in your browser, which are described in the next section.
		</p>
		<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-card border border-border">
			<table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
				<thead>
					<tr class="bg-surface-2 text-ink">
						<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-semibold">What</th>
						<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-semibold">Why</th>
						<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-semibold">Where</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
					<tr>
						<th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Your best net speed for each test length and text type</th>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">
							So the site can show you a personal best and tell you when you have beaten it.
						</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">Your browser's local storage</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Your light or dark theme choice</th>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">
							So the site keeps the theme you picked instead of following your system setting every
							time.
						</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-2.5">Your browser's local storage</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p>
			Both are removed if you clear your browser's site data, and both disappear with the browser profile.
			They are never transmitted, never linked to an account and never visible to anyone else.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Google Analytics">
		<p>
			keysprint uses Google Analytics 4, measurement ID <code class="font-mono text-sm">G-6FJT50DLSS</code>,
			to count visits and understand which pages people find useful. The measurement tag is loaded from
			<code class="font-mono text-sm">googletagmanager.com</code> on every page.
		</p>
		<p>
			Google Analytics may set first-party cookies such as <code class="font-mono text-sm">_ga</code> and
			<code class="font-mono text-sm">_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code>, and may collect technical information
			including your IP address (used to estimate approximate location), browser and device details, the
			page you arrived from, the pages you visit and how long you spend on them. Google processes this data
			under its own
			<a
				href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
				class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				target="_blank">privacy policy</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			We do not send your typing results, keystrokes or the text you type to Google Analytics. The
			analytics is there to measure page traffic, not to profile how well you type.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can block or delete analytics cookies through your browser settings, or install the
			<a
				href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
				class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				target="_blank">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a
			>. Blocking analytics does not affect the typing test, lessons or saved scores.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="What is not collected">
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-ink-subtle">
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No name, email address, phone number or account.</strong> There is no
				sign-up form anywhere on the site.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No advertising or ad tracking.</strong> There are no ads, no affiliate
				links and no advertising pixels.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No keystroke logging.</strong> Your typing is measured so that the test
				can score you, and that is all it is used for. It is not recorded, stored or transmitted.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-ink">No third-party embeds beyond analytics.</strong> There are no social
				widgets, maps or videos, and no fonts loaded from another company's servers. The only third-party
				script is the Google Analytics tag described above.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="The hosting provider">
		<p>
			keysprint is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub has to process your request in order to
			send you a page, and it may keep standard technical logs such as your IP address, the time of the
			request and the page requested, for a short period, for security and troubleshooting.
		</p>
		<p>
			That handling is done by GitHub, not by keysprint. keysprint has no access to those logs and does not
			use them for anything. The
			<a
				href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement"
				class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				target="_blank">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
			>
			explains the details.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Children">
		<p>
			keysprint is a general audience site and is not directed at children. We do not ask for personal
			information, and we do not knowingly collect it from children. The Google Analytics data described
			above is used in aggregate to understand page traffic.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Your choices">
		<p>
			You can clear the stored scores and theme through your browser's settings. Clearing your browsing
			data removes the local storage along with the analytics cookies. You can also block analytics
			cookies or use the Google Analytics opt-out add-on without affecting the typing test.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you have a question about anything on this page, the
			<a href="/contact/" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink">contact page</a> explains how
			to reach the person behind the site.
		</p>
	</ContentSection>

	<ContentSection title="Changes to this policy">
		<p>
			If this policy changes, the page will be updated and the date at the top will change with it. There
			is no list to sign up for and no notification to send, because the site does not collect an address
			to send one to.
		</p>
		<p class="text-sm text-ink-subtle">Last updated: {updated}.</p>
	</ContentSection>
</BaseLayout>
